.key VOL/A,TAG/A
.bra {
.ket }
; soak-fs VOL TAG: copy SYS:Libs to VOL:soak, hash it, delete it, until
; SHARED:sbench/soak/stop exists. Every round's MD5 list is appended to
; SHARED:sbench/soak/TAG.md5 (tools/soakcheck.py checks each round).
FailAt 30
Echo "start" >SHARED:sbench/soak/{TAG}.log
Date >>SHARED:sbench/soak/{TAG}.log
Set n 0
Lab round
Copy SYS:Libs {VOL}:soak ALL QUIET
CD {VOL}:soak
C:MD5Sum #? >>SHARED:sbench/soak/{TAG}.md5
CD RAM:
Delete {VOL}:soak ALL QUIET FORCE >NIL:
Set n `Eval $n + 1`
If NOT EXISTS SHARED:sbench/soak/stop
  Skip round BACK
EndIf
Echo "end after $n rounds" >>SHARED:sbench/soak/{TAG}.log
Date >>SHARED:sbench/soak/{TAG}.log
Echo "{TAG} done" >SHARED:sbench/soak/{TAG}.done
